# Paths that assistants and fast search tools (ripgrep, fd) should not read or index.
# Those tools already honor .gitignore, so this file holds only the delta: paths that
# are committed, or that .gitignore deliberately un-ignores, but that still have no
# business in an assistant's context.

# Env files. .gitignore un-ignores .env.example because it is the committed config
# contract, and that one is worth reading; every other .env holds real values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Committed, generated, and thousands of lines long — never worth reading in full.
uv.lock

# Belt and suspenders. .gitignore covers these too, but a key that slipped into a
# commit should still never be indexed.
*.key
*.pem
secrets/
credentials/
.ssh/
